  "instructions": [
    "Wash the napa cabbage and carefully separate the leaves, discarding the core.",
    "Blanch the leaves in a pot of salted boiling water for 30 seconds, then transfer them to ice water to stop cooking.",
    "Drain and pat the leaves dry with a towel.",
    "In a large bowl, combine cooked quinoa, roasted carrot and parsnip, dill, parsley, garlic, lemon juice, olive oil, apple cider vinegar, honey, chives, walnuts, salt, and pepper.",
    "Taste the mixture and adjust seasoning if needed.",
    "Place a spoonful of the filling onto the center of each cabbage leaf.",
    "Fold the sides of the leaf over the filling and roll tightly to secure.",
    "Serve the wraps at room temperature, optionally drizzled with a light yogurt or tahini sauce."
